{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he told.</b> This verse indicates the interpretation: Moses, and for Israel on their account." "<b>The hardship.</b> From the root of ונלאו מצרים (above, Exodus 7:18) [Egypt was exhausted]. The tav is added, and the meaning: trouble that exhausts a person to bear it or to tell of it. And the meaning concerns Egypt's pursuit at the sea, and the coming of Amalek, and their thirst — and from all of them HaShem delivered them."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:29.543146644Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}